@*
    Per-queue small-multiples view (task 11.3) — renders one `day × hour` heatmap per visible queue,
    with every small-multiple shaded using a SINGLE shared color-ramp scale spanning the global
    minimum and maximum cell values across all visible queues, so that equal values render at equal
    intensity in every small-multiple and cell intensities are directly comparable (Req 3.7).

    The shared ramp domain is the matrix's [Min, Max] (the global domain — Property 11), and the
    actual shading / contrast / keyboard + tooltip behavior is performed by the
    `window.heatmapCharts.renderPerQueue` renderer in Content/js/heatmap.js. This component only maps
    the computed HeatmapMatrix into that renderer's model and manages the JS lifecycle, following the
    same IJSRuntime interop pattern as the existing analytics charts.
*@
@namespace a2n.Hangfire.Dashboard.Components.Pages.Heatmap
@using a2n.Hangfire.Dashboard.Models

@if (!HasVisibleData)
{
    <EmptyState Icon="grid-3x3-gap"
                Message="No per-queue schedule to display."
                Subtitle="No populated cells were found for the visible queues in the selected window." />
}
else
{
    <div class="heatmap-perqueue" id="@_containerId" aria-label="Per-queue schedule small multiples"></div>
}
